---
layout: docs.njk
permalink: /docs/schemas/v0.4/dtcg-extensions/
title: DTCG token extensions — v0.4
description: JSON Schema reference for Design Lasagna governance metadata authored in DTCG $extensions under the recipes.designlasagna key.
schemaDocVersion: v0.4
schemaDocV03Href: /docs/schemas/v0.3/dtcg-extensions/
docsToc:
  - label: Start here
    href: "#start"
  - label: Token extension fields
    href: "#token-fields"
  - label: Group extension fields
    href: "#group-fields"
  - label: Supporting definitions
    href: "#definitions"
---
{%- set st = schemas.v04DtcgExtensions -%}
{%- set ref = st.ref -%}
{%- set tokenExt = ref.definitions.TokenExtensions -%}
{%- set groupExt = ref.definitions.GroupExtensions -%}

{% macro fieldTable(fields, scope) %}
<div class="schema-table-wrap">
  <table class="schema-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Field</th>
        <th>Type</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for field in fields %}
      {% set scopeDocs = schemaDocs.v04DtcgExtensions[scope] or {} %}
      {% set guide = scopeDocs[field.name] or {} %}
      <tr class="field-row">
        <td class="field-name-cell">
          <div class="field-name-toggle-wrap">
            <input class="field-toggle" id="field-details-{{ scope }}-{{ loop.index }}" type="checkbox" aria-label="Show details for {{ field.name }}">
            <label class="field-name-toggle" for="field-details-{{ scope }}-{{ loop.index }}">
              <span class="field-chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <code>{{ field.name }}{% if field.required %}<span class="required-field" aria-label="required">*</span>{% endif %}</code>
              {% if field.deprecated %}<span class="field-status field-status--deprecated">Deprecated</span>{% endif %}
            </label>
          </div>
        </td>
        <td>
          {% if field.type %}
            {% if field.type is string %}<code>{{ field.type }}</code>{% else %}<code>{{ field.type | join(', ') }}</code>{% endif %}
            {% if field.additionalProperties and field.additionalProperties.$ref %}
              {% set valueDefinition = field.additionalProperties.$ref | schemaDefinitionName %}
              <br>values: {% if valueDefinition %}<a class="schema-ref" href="#definition-{{ valueDefinition }}"><code>{{ valueDefinition }}</code></a>{% else %}<code>{{ field.additionalProperties.$ref }}</code>{% endif %}
            {% endif %}
          {% elif field.$ref %}
            {% set fieldDefinition = field.$ref | schemaDefinitionName %}
            {% if fieldDefinition %}<a class="schema-ref" href="#definition-{{ fieldDefinition }}"><code>{{ fieldDefinition }}</code></a>{% else %}<code>{{ field.$ref }}</code>{% endif %}
          {% else %}—{% endif %}
        </td>
        <td>
          {{ guide.summary or field.description or '—' }}
          {% if field.enum %}<br>Allowed: <code>{{ field.enum.values | join(', ') }}</code>{% endif %}
          {% if field.default !== undefined %}<br>Default: <code>{{ field.default }}</code>{% endif %}
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="field-details">
        <td colspan="3">
          <div class="field-details__content">
            <div>
              {% if guide.useWhen %}<p><strong>Use when:</strong> {{ guide.useWhen }}</p>{% endif %}
              {% if guide.provenance %}<p><strong>Origin:</strong> {{ guide.provenance }}</p>{% endif %}
              {% if guide.related and guide.related.length %}<p><strong>Related:</strong> {% for related in guide.related %}<code>{{ related }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>{% endif %}
            </div>
            {% if guide.example %}<div><p><strong>Example usage</strong></p><pre class="json-example"><code>{{ guide.example | jsonCode | safe }}</code></pre></div>{% endif %}
          </div>
        </td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
{% endmacro %}

<section id="start">
  <p class="eyebrow">Schemas / v0.4</p>
  <h1>DTCG token extensions</h1>
  <p class="lede">A reference for Design Lasagna metadata on DTCG tokens and groups.</p>
  {% include "schema-version-nav.njk" %}
  <p>This schema validates only the <code>recipes.designlasagna</code>
  metadata stored in the DTCG <code>$extensions</code> hook; the linked
  official <a href="https://www.designtokens.org/tr/drafts/format/">DTCG
  Format specification</a> defines the host format. It is the
  authoring-side counterpart to the resolved <a href="/docs/schemas/v0.4/tokens/">v0.4
  tokens</a> format.</p>
  <aside class="schema-install" aria-labelledby="use-dtcg-extensions-schema">
    <div class="schema-install__intro">
      <p class="schema-install__kicker">Start here</p>
      <h2 id="use-dtcg-extensions-schema">Extend a DTCG file</h2>
      <p>Add Design Lasagna governance metadata under
      <code>$extensions["recipes.designlasagna"]</code> on DTCG tokens and
      groups.</p>
    </div>
    <dl class="schema-install__sources">
      <div><dt>Schema URL</dt><dd><a href="{{ st.canonicalUrl }}">{{ st.canonicalUrl }}</a></dd></div>
      <div><dt>npm</dt><dd><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@designlasagna/schemas"><code>{{ st.npmImportPath }}</code></a></dd></div>
    </dl>
  </aside>
  <aside class="schema-docs-source" aria-label="Schema source">
    <div>
      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <p>The reference is generated from the published JSON Schema, then reviewed and extended with reader-facing guidance. It is not a substitute for the raw schema.</p>
    </div>
    <dl>
      <div><dt>Raw schema</dt><dd><a href="{{ st.canonicalUrl }}">v0.4/dtcg-extensions.json</a></dd></div>
      <div><dt>npm package</dt><dd><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@designlasagna/schemas">{{ st.npmPackage }}</a></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Repository</dt><dd><a href="https://github.com/designlasagna/schemas">designlasagna/schemas</a></dd></div>
    </dl>
  </aside>
  <h2>Minimal example</h2>
  <p>A standalone DTCG token node — only the
  <code>recipes.designlasagna</code> payload inside <code>$extensions</code>
  validates against this schema.</p>
  <pre class="json-example"><code>{{ st.minimalExample | jsonCode | safe }}</code></pre>
</section>

<section id="token-fields">
  <h2>Token extension fields</h2>
  <p>The <code>TokenExtensions</code> definition is the value of
  <code>$extensions["recipes.designlasagna"]</code> on a DTCG token. Required
  fields are marked with <code>*</code>.</p>
  {{ fieldTable(tokenExt.properties, 'TokenExtensions') }}
</section>

<section id="group-fields">
  <h2>Group extension fields</h2>
  <p>The <code>GroupExtensions</code> definition is the value of the same
  key on a DTCG group (DTCG 6.3.2). Only inheritable fields are permitted
  here, and they cascade to every descendant token unless a nearer node
  overrides them.</p>
  {{ fieldTable(groupExt.properties, 'GroupExtensions') }}
</section>

<section id="definitions">
  <h2>Supporting definitions</h2>
  <p>Reusable shapes referenced by the fields above.</p>
  <div class="schema-definition-list">
    {% for name, definition in ref.definitions | dictsort %}
      {% if name != 'TokenExtensions' and name != 'GroupExtensions' %}
      <article class="schema-definition">
        <h3 id="definition-{{ name }}"><code>{{ name }}</code></h3>
        {% set definitionGuide = schemaDocs.v04DtcgExtensions._definitions and schemaDocs.v04DtcgExtensions._definitions[name] or {} %}
        <p>{{ definitionGuide.summary or definition.description or 'See the raw schema for this definition.' }}</p>
        {% if definition.properties %}
          {{ fieldTable(definition.properties, name) }}
        {% elif definition.$ref %}
          {% set refName = definition.$ref | schemaDefinitionName %}
          {% if refName %}
            <p>Alias for <a class="schema-ref" href="#definition-{{ refName }}"><code>{{ refName }}</code></a>.</p>
          {% else %}
            <p>Reference to <code>{{ definition.$ref }}</code> in the shared v0.4 <a href="{{ schemas.v04Lifecycle.canonicalUrl }}">lifecycle fragment</a>.</p>
          {% endif %}
        {% elif definition.type %}
          <p><code>{{ definition.type }}</code>
          {% if definition.description %} — {{ definition.description }}{% endif %}
          </p>
        {% endif %}
      </article>
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<p><a href="/docs/schemas/">← All schemas</a></p>
